  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nA wave of showers and thunderstorms is expected to enter the CWA\naround 5PM and move through tonight along a quasi-lee side\nmountain trough. There is an initial chance for a downburst or\nsevere wind gust as they enter Phillips, Petroleum, or Valley\ncounty but most significant threats should be gone by about 8-9PM.\nShowers activity should exit into the Dakotas by mid-morning \nFriday. \n\nAnother set of shortwave troughs are expected on Friday afternoon\nand then Saturday through Sunday. These may have a bit more rain \nin them. The more significant trough is expected to make its way \nin this weekend, but mesoscale details are up in the air with both\nthese features as HREF Ensembles are varying widely in their form. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nOnly deviation to NBM was to PoPs Friday afternoon, as NBM had 0%\nPoP over most of the area and HREF member details have scattered \nto isolated storms. \n\nConfidence in synoptic features are moderate to high through \nSunday then moderate to low beyond. Most meso-scale features wash\nout after tonight.\n\n/GAH",
